# pytest, its coverage plugin, and numpy for wheels.yml's python-coverage job
# (roadmap VX15). Separate from requirements-coverage.txt on purpose: that lock
# is gcovr for ci.yml's C++ coverage job, and the two jobs run on different
# workflows with nothing in common but the word "coverage".
#
# numpy is here because the ac3forge wheel declares it as a runtime dependency
# and that job installs the wheel with --no-index. Without the index there is
# nowhere for pip to resolve numpy from, and WITH the index pip would be free
# to prefer a released ac3forge from PyPI over the locally built wheel the job
# exists to measure - a version comparison between a PEP 440 release and a
# setuptools_scm dev version that should not be left to chance. Satisfying the
# dependency from this lock first, then installing the wheel offline, makes
# "the wheel under test is the one the build job just produced" a property of
# the commands rather than of pip's resolution order.
#
# Regenerate the lock after any change here with:
#   python -m piptools compile --generate-hashes --strip-extras \
#     --output-file=requirements-pytest.txt requirements-pytest.in
pytest
pytest-cov
numpy
